00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:06.050 align:start position:0%
coronavirus is a global pandemic it  affects all of us and every country in  the world more than two and a half  million people have been infected so far  and we have lost almost 180,000 people  to this virus and it is still spreading  fast the response to this pandemic can  only be global we need cooperation  between governments across the world  scientists civil society business  citizens and this is why we are  organizing a global online pledging  conference on the 4th of May the aim is  to join forces and mobilize resources we  need to develop as soon as possible a  vaccine produce it and deploy to every  single corner of the world and we need  to ramp up work on prevention  diagnostics and treatments and for this  we need money so one of the main  objectives of the summit will be to  raise an initial sum of 7.5 billion euro  to kick-start the global cooperation  more will be needed in future and we  want to bring together the world and its  leaders to jointly defeat the virus I am  grateful to the experienced  organizations which are working with us  on this the global preparedness  monitoring board the Bill and Melinda  Gates Foundation the Wellcome Trust the  World Health Organization and many many  others they bring valuable expertise in  this area and I'm encouraged by the many  signs of engagement from people all over  the world  singers artists citizens sports people  business leaders we are inspired by them  and we hope that we can mobilize a  strong international response together  we are stronger and we will defeat this  virus
 

